<%- include('../partials/layout-start') %>
<%- include('../partials/page-header', { icon: 'bi-shield-check', heading: 'Privacy policy' }) %>
<section class="glass-section pb-5">
<div class="container">
  <div class="row justify-content-center"><div class="col-lg-8">
    <div class="glass-card"><div class="card-body">
      <p class="text-muted-2">Version <%= version %></p>

      <% if (!legal.isConfigured()) { %>
        <div class="alert alert-warning">
          <strong>This policy does not yet name who is responsible for your data.</strong>
          Whoever runs this site must set <code>LEGAL_CONTROLLER_NAME</code> and
          <code>LEGAL_CONTROLLER_ADDRESS</code>. Until they do, treat this site as one that
          has not finished its setup — and be careful what you give it.
        </div>
      <% } %>

      <h2 class="h6">Who is responsible</h2>
      <% if (legal.isConfigured()) { %>
        <p class="mb-1"><strong><%= legal.controller.name %></strong></p>
        <p class="text-muted-2 mb-1" style="white-space: pre-line"><%= legal.controller.address %></p>
        <% if (legal.controller.registration) { %>
          <p class="text-muted-2">Registration: <%= legal.controller.registration %></p>
        <% } %>
      <% } else { %>
        <p class="text-muted-2">Not published yet — see the notice above.</p>
      <% } %>
      <p>This site is independent and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by
         Salesforce, Inc.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">What we store, and why we are allowed to</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your account</strong> — email, name, password (stored only as a hash
            nobody can read back), and the roles you hold. Needed to give you an account at
            all: without it there is no service to provide.</li>
        <li><strong>Your profile, and anything you publish</strong> — a consultant profile, a
            job posting, a community post, a review. Published because you chose to publish
            it, and removed when you remove it.</li>
        <li><strong>Applications and messages</strong> — needed to connect the two sides of
            an application, which is what the site is for.</li>
        <li><strong>Rate figures you contribute</strong> — see below.</li>
        <li><strong>Payments</strong> — kept because tax law requires records of them to be
            kept, and for as long as it requires.</li>
        <li><strong>Where your sign-up came from</strong> — the country, derived offline from
            your IP address. The address itself is stored in binary form on your account row
            and is used for nothing else. It is destroyed when you close your account.</li>
        <li><strong>Gender and date of birth</strong> — optional, used only in aggregate,
            never shown on your profile and never shared with employers. Leaving them blank
            has no effect on anything.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="h6">How long it is kept</h2>
      <p>Your account and everything on it, for as long as the account exists — you can end
         that yourself at any time. Payment records for as long as tax law requires,
         regardless of the account. Tax-advisory enquiries are deleted on a stated schedule
         shown on that form. Nothing else is kept "just in case".</p>

      <h2 class="h6">Your rate contributions</h2>
      <p>Contributions are never displayed individually. They are aggregated with other
         people's, and no aggregate is published until at least three different people have
         contributed to it. <strong>They survive closing your account</strong>, with the link
         to you destroyed: a published benchmark that changed every time somebody left would
         be a benchmark nobody could trust, and once the link is gone the figure identifies
         nobody.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">Visitor analytics</h2>
      <p>We count page views per country per day. No path, identifier or address is kept
         alongside that count, so it cannot be traced back to a person. There is no
         third-party analytics on this site and no advertising or tracking cookie — the only
         cookie is the one that keeps you signed in.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">Who else receives it</h2>
      <% if (processors.length) { %>
        <ul>
          <% processors.forEach(function (p) { %>
            <li><strong><%= p.name %></strong> — <%= p.purpose %></li>
          <% }); %>
        </ul>
      <% } else { %>
        <p>Nobody. This deployment has no payment, email or AI service connected.</p>
      <% } %>
      <p class="text-muted-2 small">This list describes this site as it is actually running,
         not every service the software can use.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">Your rights</h2>
      <p>Two of these you can exercise yourself, immediately, without asking anybody:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>See it and take it</strong> — <a href="/profile/data">download everything
            held about your account</a> as a JSON file.</li>
        <li><strong>Erasure</strong> — <a href="/profile/close">close your account</a>. That
            page lists exactly what is destroyed and the few things that stay, with the reason
            for each.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You also have the right to have inaccurate data corrected, to object to processing,
         and to ask for it to be restricted. Most corrections you can make on your profile;
         for anything else, <a href="/contact">write to us</a>. You are entitled to an answer
         within one month.</p>
      <p>If you think we have handled your data badly you can complain to a data protection
         authority<% if (legal.controller.supervisoryAuthority) { %> —
         <%= legal.controller.supervisoryAuthority %><% } %>. You do not have to raise it with
         us first, though we would rather you did.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">Consent record</h2>
      <p>When you register we store the exact versions of these documents you accepted, and
         when. We do not record consent on your behalf for accounts created by an
         administrator. If this policy changes materially its version changes too, so your
         record says what you were actually shown rather than what is on this page today.</p>

      <h2 class="h6">Security</h2>
      <p>Passwords are hashed, never stored. The site is served over HTTPS and the session
         cookie cannot be sent over plain HTTP. Uploaded images are re-encoded rather than
         stored as you sent them, which is also what stops anything that is not an image from
         being stored at all.</p>
    </div></div>
  </div></div>
</div>
<%- include('../partials/layout-end') %>
